§ `How much would I be paid? ss 5 to 8`
-- s 5(a): arguments are the basic amount, the basic amount for a child, age, retirement age, old-age allowance, dependants allowance, spouse, children, widow, independent parent
-- a single person of 30 is in column B: 20% of 10,000
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 2000
-- a single person of 70 at retirement age: column A, 70 to under 80: 42.55%
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 70 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 4255
-- a single person of 40 paid an old-age or survivors' allowance: column A under 70: 42.14%
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 40 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 4214
-- a couple with a child, aged 60, column C: 43.5%
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 4350
-- a single person with a child at retirement age 67: 71.92% less the child amount, 7192 less 200
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 67 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 6992
-- a widow who is not an independent parent, with a child, aged 60: she fits rows 5 and 7 and the table does not choose, so the text does not say
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the same woman as an independent parent: s 5(a)(3) sends her to rows 7 and 8; as both, the same
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 4050
#ASSERT `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` 10000 200 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 4050
